Mark XVI: onboarding wizard + settings

- jarvis setup runs the onboarding wizard on demand (the wizard already
  auto-triggers on first run). setup --yes is a non-interactive CI path:
  --local, --provider, --model, --base-url; the key comes from --api-key
  or the UMBRA_API_KEY env var; live key validation is skipped; secrets
  are never echoed (masked only).
- The wizard gains an optional voice step and an optional PRO license
  activation step at the end of onboarding.
- jarvis settings show (redacted dump - keys masked, license key never
  printed), set <key>=<value> (strict dotted whitelist; brains.fallback.*
  materializes a fallback brain; secrets masked in the confirmation),
  reset [--yes] (wipes brain settings only - memories, health data and
  the license key are kept).
- settings.py holds pure helpers (apply_setting, show_text, reset_config)
  so the CLI stays thin; tests cover redaction, type coercion, whitelist
  refusal, and all non-interactive paths.
- Version 3.3.0.
